div.verse:
Be ye mild at their anger; humble at their boasting; to their blasphemies return your prayers: to their error, your  
            Be ye firm. firmness in the faith: when they are cruel, be ye gentle; not endeavouring to imitate their ways. (3 Let us be their brethren in all kindness and moderation, but let us be followers of the Lord;  
            Who has been more, etc. for who was ever more unjustly used? More destitute? More despised?)

Without him. Besides him, let nothing  
Become you. be worthy of you;  
In. for whom also I bear about these bonds, those spiritual jewels, in which I would to God that I might arise through your prayers.

And why are we not all wise, seeing we have receive the knowledge of God, which is Jesus Christ? Why  
            Are we foolishly destroyed? do we suffer ourselves foolishly to perish;  
            Not knowing. not considering the gift which the Lord has truly sent to us?

In whom  
            Whom may I enjoy. I rejoice, forasmuch as he is the subject unto his bishop as to the grace of God, and to the presbytery as to the law of Jesus Christ;  
            Apud. Vet. Lat. Interp. Glorificato Deum Patrem D. nostri Jesu Christi. I determined to write unto you.
